                <h3>Vilpa Talents Reaches International Milestone with Grammy Eligibility</h3>
                <p class="dateAesteticTitle2">By Zafira Hafiz</p>

            </div>
            <div class="col s12 m3"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col s12 m2"></div>
            <div class="col s12 m8">
                <img class="responsive-img" src="/assets/images/vilpaTalentsAds.jpg" style="border-radius: 25px ;">
                <p class="dateAesteticTitle2 center">Vilpa Films Announced Grammy Eligibility</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col s12 m2"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col s12 m2"></div>
            <div class="col s12 m8 paragraphStyleNews">
                <p class="bolderFont">
                    Artists contributing to Vilpa Films' original productions are now eligible for Grammy
                    consideration, marking another major milestone for the company's growing creative ecosystem.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Vilpa Films is proud to announce that music created by artists participating in its Vilpa Talents
                    initiative is now eligible for Grammy consideration for the <span class="bolderFont">69th Grammy
                        Awards.</span>
                </p>
                <p>
                    The milestone applies to original music created for Vilpa Films productions, including the company's
                    upcoming original animated series, Blue Shades, and The Undertone of David Jansen, the
                    internationally produced short film written and directed by Alejandro Vilpa.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Among the artists whose work is eligible for consideration are Eric Artz, Arno Madoni, and Anastasia
                    Chudo, whose performances form part of The Undertone of David Jansen. Their work may be considered
                    in eligible categories, including Best Classical Compendium and Producer of the Year, Classical,
                    subject to the Recording Academy's rules and nomination process.
                </p>
                <p>
                    "This milestone reflects exactly what Vilpa Talents was created for," said Alejandro Vilpa, Founder
                    of Vilpa Films. <br> <br> "Our goal has never been simply to produce films. It has always been to
                    create
                    opportunities for exceptional artists to build internationally recognized careers. Seeing their work
                    become Grammy-eligible is an exciting step in that journey."
                </p>
                <p>
                    The announcement follows another recent milestone for the company, with Vilpa Talents being featured
                    in Times Square, highlighting Alejandro Vilpa together with Dimitri Fontaine and Carla Aguilar
                    Lopez, the lead cast of the upcoming original animated series Blue Shades.
                </p>
                <p>As Vilpa Films continues expanding its international productions and creative partnerships, the
                    company remains committed to connecting emerging talent with opportunities on some of the world's
                    most recognized artistic stages.
                </p>
